project.description:
The project whose preview origin serves it: a project's page (Projects
spec §5.8), loaded at `/__cawco/page/<id>/` there (`projectPagePlace`);
absent for anything its session's origin serves.

CommandAck.description:
Hub → client, the command's lifecycle:
- `accepted` — validated, the target daemon reachable, dispatched;
- `applied`  — the daemon confirmed, where its protocol carries a
  confirmation today; where it does not, the hub stops at `accepted` and
  the stream event reflecting the change is the proof of application;
- `failed`   — terminal, with the reason a human can read.

stage.description:
`waiting`: the source's process holds work in flight ending it would
lose ({@link waiting}), and the job goes on by itself once that ends;
`filing`: the source's turn filing its open items (a person's Continue);
`starting`: the new session is starting.

FleetFaultCause.description:
Why one entry did not converge on a machine, named where it failed:
- `cli-too-old`: the claude CLI the sync ran is older than
  `CLAUDE_VERSION_FLOOR` (agent claude-version.ts), by its version;
- `cli-missing`: the machine has no claude CLI to run;
- `marketplace-unlinked`: a plugin's marketplace is not linked here;
- `hub-only`: a plugin of a marketplace that is a directory on the hub's
  machine, which the hub could not carry;
- `drifted`: the machine edited the copy CawCo wrote;
- `absent`: what CawCo recorded writing is no longer there;
- `unparsable`, `unwritable`: a config file it could not read, or write;
- `timed-out`: a run or a server that did not answer in time;
- `no-checkout`: bound to a project this machine has no checkout of;
- `missing-bytes`: the hub named a version and sent no files for it;
- `unsafe-path`: a file the hub sent names a path outside its directory;
- `unknown`: anything else, said as it was in `detail`.

LinkMode.description:
`record`: the task's fields are one record with it (the file's `issue:`,
the tracker sync's). The rest are GitHub's and Linear's own link words;
a URL a person or session writes into `links:` is `related`.

message_id.description:
The id the harness stores the message being written under, where it
stores it while it is written (opencode): what {@link STREAM_SO_FAR}
names, so a stored copy of the same message is not drawn beside it.

summary.description:
What will happen and why, in one line: "Change the fleet's CLAUDE.md";
for a shell call, the session's own reason for it ("Check whether the
two commits are on origin/main"), its command under it in `command`.

by.description:
`attempt`: its live attempt carries on, your note in hand; `start`: an
attempt starts there (the stage's `runs:`, or the project's dispatch);
`nobody`: it waits in a todo stage, nobody on it until someone starts it.

routineStarters.description:
What an empty Routines page offers to ask Caw for: what the project
repeats or waits on, as routines (project-starters.ts), in that order;
none while Jev is off.

starters.description:
What an empty board and Caw's panel offer to say to him: written for the
project from what it holds now (project-starters.ts), in that order;
none while Jev is off.

StartersChangedFrame.description:
Hub-originated: a project's starters for one place were written again;
the whole set, in its order (empty when none is offered, Jev off
included).

TailnetHttpsState.description:
Where it stands on the hub's machine:
- `absent`: no Tailscale there (no CLI, or its daemon is not running);
- `signed-out`: Tailscale is there but not signed in to a tailnet;
- `needs`: on a tailnet, and a step of the person's stands between it
  and HTTPS ({@link TailnetHttpsTodo});
- `serving`: the dashboard and the previews answer over HTTPS on the name.

TailnetHttpsStep.description:
A step of the person's on the path to HTTPS:
- `enable-magicdns`, `enable-https`: the tailnet has no certificates yet;
  both are switches on the admin console's DNS page (MagicDNS first,
  "Configure HTTPS", tailscale.com/kb/1153/enabling-https);
- `operator`: Tailscale gives its certificate only to root and its
  operator ("cert access denied", ipn/localapi/cert.go);
- `userspace`: tailscaled runs with `--tun=userspace-networking`, so the
  machine has no tailnet address to listen on;
- `port`: a listener the hub can't share holds a port on the tailnet
  address (the dashboard's socket from before it shared its port).

